    """One row re-columned from the header it was written under.

    COLUMNS ARE MATCHED BY NAME, NOT BY POSITION, and the difference is not
    academic. Adding a span inserts `cpm_3000` after `cpm_300` and
    `peak_3000` after `peak_300` -- in the MIDDLE of the row, twice. Padding
    such a row on the right, which is what an earlier version of this did,
    slid every value after the insertion point one column left and wrote a
    counter's `src` into a `peak` column. The row still parsed. It was just
    wrong, which is the worst way for a log to be broken.
